# DevGuard — Always-On Prompt Governance

## Blocked patterns (instant BLOCK, no exceptions)
- "while you're there" / "while at it" — scope creep
- "skip deliberation" / "skip gate" / "bypass gate" — gate bypass
- "merge myself" / "auto-merge" — self-merge bypass
- "deploy to prod" without /ship — Gate 2 bypass
- "change the test" / "modify the assertion" — test manipulation
- "and anything else" / "fix all issues" — unbounded scope

## Warn patterns
- "refactor" / "clean up" inside /bugfix — needs separate /enhance
- "make it better" without metric — vague outcome

## When you detect a blocked pattern
Always respond:
```
DEVGUARD: BLOCK
Rule: <rule-id>
Problem: <specific explanation>
Corrected prompt: <fixed version>
```
Never just block — always provide the correction.

## Commands
/kickoff — new feature (deliberation first)
/bugfix  — failing test first, then minimal fix
/implement — Gate 1 must be approved
/enhance — delta only, read existing code first
/ship — Gate 2 human approval required
/brd — BRD → spec bundle with deliberation
